---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Optimization sketch"
  title="Fit the density at target samples, then update its parameters"
  caption="Circular contours show the notebook's target P = N((-5, -5), I) and initial model Q = N((0, 0), I). The direction arrow is schematic, not a recorded training trajectory. The computation loop expands the handwritten backward and optimizer arrows on pages 19–20."
>
  <div class="fit-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 300 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="gaussian-fit-cloud-title gaussian-fit-cloud-desc">
      <title id="gaussian-fit-cloud-title">Initial Gaussian model and fixed target</title>
      <desc id="gaussian-fit-cloud-desc">A target with mean minus five in both coordinates and identity covariance is below and left of an initial standard-normal model. Updating the mean moves the model toward the target. The covariance is trainable too; this schematic is not an optimization result.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="gaussian-fit-cloud-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrowhead" />
        </marker>
        <marker id="gaussian-fit-update-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="accent-head" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="150" y="21" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-heading">Fixed target, trainable model</text>
      <g class="axis" marker-end="url(#gaussian-fit-cloud-arrow)">
        <path d="M 35 98 L 274 98" />
        <path d="M 198 259 L 198 47" />
      </g>
      <text x="275" y="116" class="axis-label">x₁</text>
      <text x="213" y="76" class="axis-label">x₂</text>
      <g class="tick">
        <path d="M 98 94 L 98 102" />
        <path d="M 194 198 L 202 198" />
      </g>
      <text x="98" y="118" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">−5</text>
      <text x="187" y="203" text-anchor="end" class="muted">−5</text>
      <text x="211" y="120" class="muted">0</text>
      <g class="target-contours">
        <circle cx="98" cy="198" r="20" />
        <circle cx="98" cy="198" r="40" />
      </g>
      <circle cx="98" cy="198" r="2.5" class="target-point" />
      <text x="55" y="255" class="density-label">P: μ = (−5, −5)</text>
      <g class="model-contours">
        <circle cx="198" cy="98" r="20" />
        <circle cx="198" cy="98" r="40" />
      </g>
      <circle cx="198" cy="98" r="2.5" class="model-point" />
      <text x="116" y="43" class="model-label">Q initially: μ = (0, 0)</text>
      <path d="M 170 131 C 157 165, 146 188, 127 202" class="update" marker-end="url(#gaussian-fit-update-arrow)" />
      <text x="210" y="168" class="model-label">fit μ, L</text>
      <text x="150" y="298" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Both initial covariances: I</text>
    </svg>

    <svg viewBox="0 0 300 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="gaussian-fit-loop-title gaussian-fit-loop-desc">
      <title id="gaussian-fit-loop-title">Forward computation and parameter update</title>
      <desc id="gaussian-fit-loop-desc">Trainable mean and Cholesky parameters construct a Gaussian model. Target samples enter its log-density, whose negative average is the loss. Backward computes gradients; the optimizer updates the parameters and the loop repeats.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="gaussian-fit-loop-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrowhead" />
        </marker>
        <marker id="gaussian-fit-backward-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="accent-head" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="150" y="21" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-heading">One optimization step</text>
      <rect x="39" y="42" width="222" height="50" rx="5" class="box" />
      <text x="150" y="64" text-anchor="middle">θ = (μ, a, b, c)</text>
      <text x="150" y="82" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Construct Q with Σ = LLᵀ</text>
      <path d="M 150 94 L 150 126" class="axis" marker-end="url(#gaussian-fit-loop-arrow)" />
      <rect x="39" y="130" width="222" height="50" rx="5" class="box" />
      <text x="150" y="151" text-anchor="middle">log qθ(xᵢ), xᵢ ∼ P</text>
      <text x="150" y="169" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Evaluate at fixed observations</text>
      <path d="M 150 182 L 150 214" class="axis" marker-end="url(#gaussian-fit-loop-arrow)" />
      <rect x="39" y="218" width="222" height="45" rx="5" class="loss-box" />
      <text x="150" y="246" text-anchor="middle">loss = −mean(log qθ(xᵢ))</text>
      <path d="M 263 241 C 289 241, 286 69, 265 68" class="update" marker-end="url(#gaussian-fit-backward-arrow)" />
      <text x="150" y="295" text-anchor="middle" class="model-label">backward() → optimizer.step()</text>
      <text x="150" y="314" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Gradients flow back to θ</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .fit-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 350px; height: auto; margin-inline: auto; overflow: visible; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px; }
  .panel-heading { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .axis-label { font-size: 15px; font-style: italic; }
  .axis, .tick, .arrowhead { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .target-contours { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .target-point { fill: var(--ink); }
  .model-contours { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .model-point { fill: var(--accent); }
  .model-label { fill: var(--accent); font-size: 13px; }
  .density-label { font-size: 13px; }
  .update, .accent-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .box { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .loss-box { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .fit-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
</style>
